Vroom, ooooh. The car won't start.

01:13:35.744 --> 01:13:40.404
I told the pastor: "That car over there, the one that started, won't move." I said: "The car is going to move."

01:13:40.424 --> 01:13:51.604
He said, "That car, you'll move it." I told the pastor, I said, "As for me, I bought that car with my own money." The person who had helped me a little was Patrick Sias, I think, with H&M.

01:13:51.624 --> 01:13:53.624
They put a little money inside to help me.

01:13:53.644 --> 01:13:55.344
May God bless them wherever they are.

01:13:55.364 --> 01:13:56.184
I said:

01:13:56.204 --> 01:13:59.384
I didn't take a single franc from Impact Church.

01:13:59.404 --> 01:14:09.204
I didn't take the tithe from Impact Church or the offering to buy it. It's my salary. He says: "The car, it wi—" The pastors are there, they're following me. I said: "The car, it wi-will run in the name of Jesus."

01:14:09.224 --> 01:14:15.004
Bro, the car was running like a little dog we hit. [imitates a dog] So,

01:14:15.024 --> 01:14:25.614
You can't get there at twenty kilometers an hour. I knew it like that, slowly, slowly, slowly, slowly, slowly, slowly, slowly. About a hundred kilometers like that. A hole, it takes.

01:14:25.634 --> 01:14:32.974
[moan] There, the woman outside told me—already, he was saying no, why don't we go back? Because that's very dangerous. Where we're going, it's too far. It's a road where there are...

01:14:32.994 --> 01:14:37.164
There are, a lot of accidents, people die, maillent, you know, huh? Big liboulle, all that.

01:14:37.184 --> 01:14:41.434
I said: That car will leave; we won't abort the tri-, the trip.

01:14:41.454 --> 01:14:47.344
Well, I saw the demons who now wanted to block our way of bringing salvation to the brothers.

01:14:47.364 --> 01:14:55.084
We arrived there very late. So, we even called the mechanic to, uh, check the car.

01:14:55.104 --> 01:15:00.464
I parked it right up against the wall where I was preaching. There was an anointing in that room that day.

01:15:00.484 --> 01:15:03.744
We preached, prayed, papap, we cast out the demons.

01:15:03.764 --> 01:15:08.674
When we're finished, bam, around four o'clock, we have to go back to Kinshasa.

01:15:08.694 --> 01:15:10.244
About three hundred kilometers.

01:15:10.264 --> 01:15:13.284
These aren't roads like the highway here. You, you can see the highway.

01:15:13.304 --> 01:15:17.144
Don't even look at the na-na-national in your neighborhood.

01:15:17.164 --> 01:15:19.904
There, it's just roads, roads.

01:15:19.924 --> 01:15:22.084
That's what's serious.

01:15:22.104 --> 01:15:24.453
What matters, I said: There is no need to say thank you, because you are a good God.

01:15:24.473 --> 01:15:28.524
You know, when we'd left Kikwit, we would get back around three o'clock.

01:15:28.544 --> 01:15:36.964
Four o'clock, three o'clock, brother. On small roads, lots of trees, big forests. At night it's dark, so you need light to be able to walk. We were driving at seventy-four,

01:15:36.984 --> 01:15:39.624
Because we don't know what's ahead over there, brother.

01:15:39.644 --> 01:15:46.584
I told myself: When I arrived in Kinshasa, the next day, Saturday. I arrived on Friday. On Saturday, I left quickly.

01:15:46.604 --> 01:15:50.244
I left to bless Élysée's wedding. You see, huh? For Élysée's wedding.

01:15:50.264 --> 01:15:57.384
When we had finished blessing, around midnight, I said to my wife: "Let's go out—because we're going to pray in Kinshasa. Let's go."

01:15:57.404 --> 01:16:02.984
That Sunday, with Boni over there. We had two cars, with Oya too, right. You were in the front; (I was) in the car behind.

01:16:03.004 --> 01:16:13.584
So, we were in Mom Julie's car, huh, Mom Julie. I was in the car with— all the cars were full. Brother, we arrived in the middle of a place where there are too many military camps, those Congolese bandits there.

01:16:13.604 --> 01:16:19.984
Hand baby. They say that if the car breaks down over there, you should run away right away, because there you're, you're in trouble. The car broke down.

01:16:20.004 --> 01:16:30.244
I say: It's five hundred meters from the, the "cachets de barge." I said: That's not good. We pushed it a bit [imitates the car] to get over there. Tire, tire crushed. Brother,

01:16:30.264 --> 01:16:35.504
I said: "It's not a big deal, we've got tires." So, there were a lot of us, huh. About ten. We really put the tires on.

01:16:35.524 --> 01:16:38.644
Brother, we're going to look at my s-, my spare tire.

01:16:38.664 --> 01:16:41.004
It was already screwed up a long time ago.

01:16:41.024 --> 01:16:45.864
But then I thought to myself: What if it happened to Bandu, in Bandundu, in that forest over there?

01:16:45.884 --> 01:16:55.724
To say that, my brother, when we walk with God, always, he pro— he protects us. God said to the angel: "Angel, you, get into the tire, stay inside."

01:16:55.744 --> 01:16:56.884
So be it, you become a tire.

01:16:56.904 --> 01:17:04.204
When he gets to the Congo, now, to Kinshasa, now, let him get a flat so he can see that no, he doesn't have a spare tire.

01:17:04.224 --> 01:17:06.724
[acclamation] But what is serious, brother.

01:17:06.744 --> 01:17:13.484
Boni is online; she—she's back, the one who was with me. Brother, what shocked me a lot was the outside too.

01:17:13.504 --> 01:17:24.684
When we finished the meeting there, where the car had arrived with a lot of difficulty, huh. Brother, when I started the car, when [vroom] the car started, brother. Brother, I drove at one hundred seventy kilometers an hour.

01:17:24.704 --> 01:17:26.844
Brother, the car was moving like an airplane.

01:17:26.864 --> 01:17:33.484
I thought to myself: That car just went in for service, we washed everything. Man, the car drove off.

01:17:33.504 --> 01:17:35.263
It was on, on Saturday, huh.

01:17:35.283 --> 01:17:40.264
Well, we arrived home that Saturday. We went to Maluku, we ate, and then we went back home.

01:17:40.284 --> 01:17:42.264
Sunday, kilt.

01:17:42.284 --> 01:17:52.344
Sunday morning, between—uh—eleven p.m. and two a.m., I started it again. Bas Congo, we were, we were eight people, uh, eleven cars.

01:17:52.364 --> 01:17:59.804
The car was running like a plane. I said: "But that breakdown—who fixed it again?" Brother, have faith.

01:17:59.824 --> 01:18:05.164
When you want to do something, you must—you feel a lot of, of obstacles; don't give in quickly.

01:18:05.184 --> 01:18:08.564
[acclamation] Resist the Di-, the devil.

01:18:08.584 --> 01:18:11.724
[amen] I was going to— you know, in Kenge, we won.

01:18:11.744 --> 01:18:21.304
In Kenge, we got the mayor of Kenge, a member of Nayot, the comman-, a commander of Kenge's security. So in Kenge, we only got tough, tough people who are pastors, huh.

01:18:21.324 --> 01:18:26.644
So calling off that trip was the devil.

01:18:26.664 --> 01:18:29.204
[amen] You are unnecessary.

01:18:29.224 --> 01:18:33.074
There are spirits, as we've seen, who do all that work.

01:18:33.094 --> 01:18:34.524
They need to be watched.

01:18:34.544 --> 01:18:39.624
You believe that? Say amen. [amen] The number-one mandate of a shepherd,

01:18:39.644 --> 01:18:52.284
So, as a pastor, my job is to shepherd the flock — the sheep like you. I must teach you well, pray for you, guide you, talk with you. Don't marry that man.

01:18:52.304 --> 01:18:58.684
He's a crook. Marry with— that's my mandate. When I tell you: Don't marry that boy, don't argue about it. Obey me, it's me, brother.

01:18:58.704 --> 01:19:06.324
I can see a ma— a husband who's a crook. Brother, I had banned all the people of Impact Church who are married to crooks.

01:19:06.344 --> 01:19:11.264
Bro, nobody—they're all here, right. They say, "I didn't say anything." I said, "That one,"

01:19:11.284 --> 01:19:26.516
No. Because you, when you fall in love, you're like distracted people, and all that. The demon can get into a man, it seduces you, then you leave, and then tomorrow, now, you become a punching bag where people hit to build their muscles.

01:19:26.536 --> 01:19:31.016
Or we'll come back — someone is going to get off the boat in the evening.

01:19:31.036 --> 01:19:34.596
You bring me a boy, I say: "That boy — leave him, leave him, leave him there." He walks by.

01:19:34.616 --> 01:19:36.996
I can read through the Spirit of God.

01:19:37.016 --> 01:19:41.176
That's a bad man, a bad woman. I can read that, brother.

01:19:41.196 --> 01:19:42.656
Say amen.

01:19:42.676 --> 01:19:52.146
No one is perfect. We can make mistakes, but brother, in eight out of ten cases I can tell the fake from the real. A shepherd's number one duty is to tend the flock.

01:19:52.166 --> 01:20:00.736
When you meet a boy, why, why, why do you keep it secret? Tell the pastor about it, won't you?

01:20:00.756 --> 01:20:09.036
When things go wrong, you come into the office [laughs]. I have brothers—many of them—they came into the office because it all fell apart.

01:20:09.056 --> 01:20:11.536
They're—many are over there, I know.

01:20:11.556 --> 01:20:16.056
Don't wait for someone to hurt you.

01:20:16.076 --> 01:20:22.176
Brother, a true pastor loves God. When people mistreat his spiritual children, he suffers.

01:20:22.196 --> 01:20:34.476
Whenever people have harmed members of the Church, brother, you can't talk about it enough, and I'm angry. If you put me alone with that boy in secret, I'll beat him very, very badly — but in a way that won't leave any swelling.

01:20:34.496 --> 01:20:36.376
Now, look.

01:20:36.396 --> 01:20:48.216
The number one mandate of sheep, or of flocks, is to know the voice of their shepherd and to follow. When he speaks, he speaks. That's the principle here.

01:20:48.236 --> 01:20:49.416
That's the principle over there.

01:20:49.436 --> 01:20:59.376
Since you've been here at Impact, who do you listen to? Who is your shepherd or your pa—your pastor? Romans chapter twelve, verse two:

01:20:59.396 --> 01:21:16.736
Do not conform yourselves to the present age, but be transformed by the renewal of your mind so that you may discern what is the will of God, what is good,

01:21:16.756 --> 01:21:25.896
pleasant and pa-- and perfect. Brother, without the renewal of your mindset, you will not discover what God's will is for your life.

01:21:25.916 --> 01:21:38.276
What is good in my life? Which decision should I make? What is pleasant? What is perfect? You will keep fumbling, going in circles; you'll fall into confusion, and then you'll end up making bad decisions.

01:21:38.296 --> 01:21:43.296
But renewal makes God's will clear in your life.

01:21:43.316 --> 01:21:48.776
Now, look. I've written the same verses again, but differently.

01:21:48.796 --> 01:21:54.336
Do not imitate the behaviors and customs of this world.

01:21:54.356 --> 01:21:55.716
It's the same verse, huh:

01:21:55.736 --> 01:22:00.516
Do not copy the behaviors and customs of this world.

01:22:00.536 --> 01:22:09.496
But let God transform you into a new person by changing the way you do what? Thinking.

01:22:09.516 --> 01:22:19.116
So, you will learn to know whose will? God's toward you, and it is good, pleasing and per-- and perfect.

01:22:19.136 --> 01:22:28.116
Another version says: Don't let yourself be molded into the same mold that the whole world has been molded into.

01:22:28.136 --> 01:22:34.336
But be renewed in your thinking. In fact, look, that is where man's struggle lies.

01:22:34.356 --> 01:22:40.356
It's good that you became a Christian, but that's not enough. You must go further. Now, look at the children of God.

01:22:40.376 --> 01:22:41.036
Now, look.

01:22:41.056 --> 01:22:56.076
There are a lot of things in this verse. Let's make some, let's make some connections. A) Being a new creature or a new person requires that we be able to change our way of thinking and of seeing things.

01:22:56.096 --> 01:22:58.876
This is the first thing.

01:22:58.896 --> 01:23:07.376
What you have there, Adjang, Évariste, Philippe Kom, that way of seeing things, is not what God wants. It's wrong.

01:23:07.396 --> 01:23:09.276
That's incorrect.

01:23:09.296 --> 01:23:17.216
It's Babylon, it's the world, it's television, it's the university that put us in a hole,

01:23:17.236 --> 01:23:27.276
It forged us in its own way. Don't let yourselves be molded into the same mold the world rented — in elementary school, secondary school, university, at work, on TV.

01:23:27.296 --> 01:23:30.616
They're forcing us into the same mold.

01:23:30.636 --> 01:23:37.116
It's, it's intentional. Now, now, even via our own phones. I'll talk about it next week. B ] The need that is wished for,

01:23:37.136 --> 01:23:54.816
The need, which is God's wish, is that each person know God's will for himself and for the community. You should know that, brother. And if I ask you the question: Do you want to know God's will for your life and community?

01:23:54.836 --> 01:24:04.336
What will your answer be? How will or should the answer be? Yes.

01:24:04.356 --> 01:24:06.116
Nothing else.

01:24:06.136 --> 01:24:07.556
Now, look.

01:24:07.576 --> 01:24:12.856
Change the way you see and think.

01:24:12.876 --> 01:24:17.036
And there is the key to knowing whose will it is: God's.

01:24:17.056 --> 01:24:22.056
Changing your way of seeing and thinking becomes the key to knowing the will of God.

01:24:22.076 --> 01:24:30.636
Changing the way you see things allows your mind to be renewed by the word of God.

01:24:30.656 --> 01:24:41.196
Remember that you don't know who you are or how to be and live until you've read the word of whom? God's.

01:24:41.216 --> 01:24:48.336
It is the word of God that shapes us. And our true identity is hidden in Christ, in the word of God.

01:24:48.356 --> 01:24:55.496
By reading the Bible, we download and install God's word within us.

01:24:55.516 --> 01:25:01.356
And it eventually changes the way we think and reason.

01:25:01.376 --> 01:25:14.176
He who neglects and does not read the Word will remain Babylonian, pagan, spiritually worldly—spiritually worldly in the seminaries and in the church.

01:25:14.196 --> 01:25:31.728
And do you see that? Worldly, spiritual Babylon in the church and in, in the seminaries. That's what the devil wants. How many among us have already prayed for a change of mentality? We say to God: "I want to know the will,

01:25:31.748 --> 01:25:37.188
"the will of—your will." That's the basis for getting there. In the meantime, it's very simple.

01:25:37.208 --> 01:25:42.028
Start, start by changing how you think and by reflecting.

01:25:42.048 --> 01:25:48.168
His, his will will ap-, will be apparent or visible automatically.

01:25:48.188 --> 01:25:50.708
Tell me: "I understand."

01:25:50.728 --> 01:25:56.168
One last point. Let's talk a little about the problem of knowing whose will it is — God's.

01:25:56.188 --> 01:25:57.928
Look.

01:25:57.948 --> 01:26:12.008
There is a connection between knowing God's will for your life and for your community and having your thoughts changed or renewed. Since knowing God's will becomes a utopia if you don't do the work of changing menta-,

01:26:12.028 --> 01:26:16.088
mentality.

01:26:16.108 --> 01:26:27.588
Do you think I was going to come and set up a system, a closed group with everyone who—who lives over there if I—if I hadn't had a shift in mindset? That's what brought that about.

01:26:27.608 --> 01:26:39.808
The titanic work I have always done during the years of changing my mentality. I don't want to be Babylonian, to think differently, to be, to be a client, especially a-, different airplanes, to be a different Francist.

01:26:39.828 --> 01:26:44.948
That's what made me see things differently, very differently.

01:26:44.968 --> 01:26:46.948
It's really important to get that.

01:26:46.968 --> 01:26:49.148
Now, look.

01:26:49.168 --> 01:26:50.308
Look.

01:26:50.328 --> 01:27:03.128
One can say that God's will equals the grace that knows the paths to tomorrows.

01:27:03.148 --> 01:27:04.668
I've explained it below.

01:27:04.688 --> 01:27:18.108
God's will is your next decision to go left or right, rather than thinking about God's will on the basis that I will be X or Y in the future.

01:27:18.128 --> 01:27:22.468
That's not the way to talk about God's will.

01:27:22.488 --> 01:27:24.568
Many people think that way.

01:27:24.588 --> 01:27:31.588
Lord, show me God's will. What should I do? X or Y tomorrow. That's not the way to discover God's will.

01:27:31.608 --> 01:27:43.888
No, brother. Now, look at me. Look at me. God's will for your life is your correct decision about what you are going to do tomorrow to stay on the right path that God had already prepared for,

01:27:43.908 --> 01:27:50.948
for you.

01:27:50.968 --> 01:28:06.258
If every day you say "tomorrow," what does God want me to do? I wake up in the morning, pray, help a brother, go to church. When you know that, do you understand? When you know what God expects of you tomorrow,

01:28:06.278 --> 01:28:15.148
Because you've already made a change of mindset; that's what will, little by little, at each step, lead you to discover whose will? God's. The more you progress, the more you'll discover it.

01:28:15.168 --> 01:28:21.728
Because the Word tells us: when the Holy Spirit comes, he will lead us.

01:28:21.748 --> 01:28:27.308
He will lead us to discover the will of God. Now, look, in closing.

01:28:27.328 --> 01:28:41.528
If we understand God's will, it takes away a lot of confusion and muddle. There's too much muddle in your head, because God's will is a path, an evolving journey. You evolve.

01:28:41.548 --> 01:28:44.188
Now, look.

01:28:44.208 --> 01:28:46.748
The path to the end.

01:28:46.768 --> 01:28:52.328
Only grace knows the path that leads you to the end. That is eternity without end, here.

01:28:52.348 --> 01:28:53.688
That's grace, right there.

01:28:53.708 --> 01:28:55.018
You want to go here.

01:28:55.038 --> 01:28:57.668
But the only thing that matters here is the grace of God.

01:28:57.688 --> 01:29:06.508
When you are defiled by sins, grace moves away. It is grace that, it is grace that shows the ways to get here.

01:29:06.528 --> 01:29:17.528
Find the way through cries, through crises. When in your life, your life, there are crises, there are struggles, there are difficulties, there are rejections, there are deaths. Don't see only the negative side.

01:29:17.548 --> 01:29:26.648
But if you're meditating, reflecting, when I say, "Wait for me," it will push you to surrender yourself into the hands of gra—, of grace. You say that I myself can do nothing.

01:29:26.668 --> 01:29:35.108
You are going to surrender yourself here and he—he will allow you to go toward... eternity, toward... your destiny. Now, look. Last sentence here.

01:29:35.128 --> 01:29:48.768
One can say that your way of thinking, of how to discover and know the way of God in these times, in these sick and crazy times we are living in, which are carrying us straight toward the end,

01:29:48.788 --> 01:29:58.128
God is emphasizing the integration of the Word of God into our lives and our thou-, our thoughts. We must-- Say after me:

01:29:58.148 --> 01:30:04.878
I serve your word. I serve your word. In my heart. In my heart. So as not to sin against you.

01:30:04.898 --> 01:30:06.388
So as not to sin against you. Amen.

01:30:06.408 --> 01:30:13.898
[calm musical outro]
